{
  "tickets": [
    {
      "id": "gen-021",
      "subject": "Pharmacy is rejecting alternative fills",
      "body": "Every time the local pharmacy tells us a drug is out of stock, trying to switch the patient over to a therapeutic alternative is a total nightmare in the system. Why is this workflow so hidden and difficult to figure out?"
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-022",
      "subject": "Creating a standard lab panel bundle",
      "body": "Good morning. We are trying to group several of our routine blood tests together into a single requisition bundle for our annual wellness exams. Could you please let us know how to set up this custom panel so all of our providers can easily select it from their order menus?"
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-023",
      "subject": "Question regarding user role adjustments and permissions audit",
      "body": "Hello support team, I am terribly sorry to bother you with this administrative task, but we are currently reviewing our internal security setup across our large provider network. I need to restrict access to certain sensitive financial ledgers and make sure our billing staff only see what is necessary. Could someone please guide me through auditing our custom permission levels and updating the user roles accordingly? Thank you so much for your time and assistance."
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-024",
      "subject": "Outside lab uploads failing",
      "body": "Can't upload outside lab PDFs to patient charts right now. The upload tool keeps throwing an error for everyone in the clinic."
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-025",
      "subject": "Patient online scheduling showing wrong appointment types",
      "body": "We set up the portal for patients to book their own visits online, but somehow all the restricted procedure types are showing up as available for anyone to pick. How do I limit what patients can select on the web widget?"
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-026",
      "subject": "Procedure for routing abnormal results to covering physicians",
      "body": "Dear support, we are reviewing our internal administrative workflows for incoming laboratory diagnostics. Could you provide documentation on how to route specific abnormal lab flags to a covering physician when the primary provider is out of the office?"
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-027",
      "subject": "Medication out of stock alerts",
      "body": "How are we supposed to handle pharmacy messages when a drug isn't available? I can't find where to swap the prescription out."
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-028",
      "subject": "Adjusting text message reminder timing for patients",
      "body": "Hello, we are hoping to tweak when our automated appointment reminder texts go out to patients ahead of their visits. Right now they seem to go out 24 hours prior, but we would like to test pushing that to 48 hours with a slightly different wording. Could you let me know where in the settings we can modify both the schedule and the content template for these messages?"
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-029",
      "subject": "Reminder texts not going out and patients are missing visits",
      "body": "I am at my wit's end trying to figure out why half of my patients aren't getting their automated text and email reminders for their appointments. I checked the settings page and everything looks enabled, but three people no-showed this week alone because they claim nothing ever popped up on their phones. I need someone to look into why these messages are failing to deliver immediately, because this is costing us time and money."
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-030",
      "subject": "Help with misapplied insurance remittance payments",
      "body": "Hello, I am so sorry to reach out with a billing issue, but I made a mistake while posting an electronic remittance advice batch this morning and accidentally applied a large insurance payment across the wrong invoice lines for a couple of accounts. Could someone please help me figure out the proper way to back out these misapplied entries and redistribute the funds correctly without messing up our end-of-month reconciliation reports? I really appreciate your patience and guidance."
    }
  ]
}
